From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karthik Siruvalam <karthik@nexthop.ai>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:10:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] teamd: state: match a per-port item path on the full port
 name

__find_by_item_path() resolves the port in ports.<ifname>.<subpath> with
strncmp(tdport->ifname, token, strlen(token)), i.e. a prefix match. If
another member of the same team has a longer name that starts with the
requested one and comes first in the port list, the item is read from or
written to the wrong port: on a team with veth_a and veth_a2,

    teamdctl team0 state item set ports.veth_a.runner.macsec_gate false

flipped veth_a2. SONiC member names make this realistic (Ethernet4 vs
Ethernet40, Ethernet12 vs Ethernet120 in the same PortChannel), and
runner.macsec_gate is driven by teammgr through this path. Require the
port name length to match as well.

Signed-off-by: Karthik Siruvalam <karthik@nexthop.ai>
---
 teamd/teamd_state.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/teamd/teamd_state.c b/teamd/teamd_state.c
index 0714880..07008fe 100644
--- a/teamd/teamd_state.c
+++ b/teamd/teamd_state.c
@@ -318,7 +318,11 @@ static int __find_by_item_path(struct teamd_state_val_item **p_item,
 		subpath = ifname_end + 1;
 
 		teamd_for_each_tdport(cur_tdport, ctx) {
-			if (!strncmp(cur_tdport->ifname, ifname_start,
+			/* Full-name match: a plain strncmp over ifname_len would
+			 * also accept any longer port name that merely starts
+			 * with the requested one (Ethernet4 vs Ethernet40). */
+			if (strlen(cur_tdport->ifname) == ifname_len &&
+			    !strncmp(cur_tdport->ifname, ifname_start,
 				     ifname_len)) {
 				tdport = cur_tdport;
 				break;
